# behavior: a module-scoped `yield` fixture is set up once for its file and torn down after the file's last test, and a session-scoped fixture is set up once on its first use, in one process, as 0.5.1 runs them (#3149).
# cli-commands:
#   test tests/test_scopes.incn --nocapture
# expect-stdout:
#
#   running 1 test
#   module setup
#   session setup
#   first test
#   test_scopes.incn::test_first PASSED
#   second test
#   module teardown
#   test incan_case_group ... ok
#
#   test result: ok. 1 passed; 0 failed; 0 ignored; 0 measured; 0 filtered out; finished in <duration>
#
#   test_scopes.incn::test_second PASSED

def main() -> None:
    println("main")
